<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s15(1)(e)> tmk:authorityStatus tmk:NotHeld ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s15(1)(e)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s168> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Object of Part"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:47781cb02b0c5745e7dbba4342550ac55494f1833919e3d795b7666f64036aa3" ;
    tmk:text "This Part: (a) defines a certification trade mark; and (b) provides to what extent, and subject to what modifications or additions, the provisions of this Act relating to trade marks apply to certification trade marks; and (c) outlines the role of the Commission in the regulation of certification trade marks." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s168" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s16E> tmk:authorityStatus tmk:NotHeld ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s16E" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s180> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Assignment of registered certification trade mark"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:3b46a8b274ddfe758b1587e4fd281bb524bb60fecba5f6e1d16d21f50c57f354" ;
    tmk:text "(1) A registered certification trade mark may be assigned only with the consent of the Commission. (2) An application to the Commission for its consent to the assignment of a registered certification trade mark must be in accordance with the regulations. (3) In deciding whether or not to give its consent, the Commission must have regard to the matters provided for under the regulations. (4) An application may be made to the Administrative Review Tribunal for the review of a decision of the Commission refusing to give its consent." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s180" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s23(4)> tmk:authorityStatus tmk:NotHeld ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s23(4)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s28> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Application by joint owners"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:4f5add8c95ec77436881c6e59a8fc9fec8b8b074cb1419ad5f2c74cc186b1eb8" ;
    tmk:text "If the relations between 2 or more persons interested in a trade mark are such that none of them is entitled to use the trade mark except: (a) on behalf of all of them; or (b) in relation to goods and/or services with which all of them are connected in the course of trade; the persons may together apply for its registration under subsection 27(1)." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s28" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s29(1)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s29> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:2016d0c74cdc8bfb58951144ada28ba147cd9659396b57d30a4becbd26994b23" ;
    tmk:ordinal 1 ;
    tmk:text "(1) If:" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s29(1)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s35> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Appeal"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:ecf843a502d95cd02974fec8a61c0e86740818500621aa5710a5c9c4ffb34fd0" ;
    tmk:text "The applicant may appeal to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) against a decision of the Registrar: (a) to accept the application subject to conditions or limitations; or (b) to reject the application. Note: For applicant see section 6." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s35" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s37> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Lapsing of application if not accepted in time"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:751a181c0ed5176ef8513fac1e190a3c07959f57f864c9deec225799c449d141" ;
    tmk:text "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an application lapses if it is not accepted within the prescribed period or within that period as extended in accordance with the regulations. (2) If, after the prescribed period or the prescribed period as extended (as the case may be) has expired, the Registrar extends under section 224 the period within which the application may be accepted, the application: (a) is taken not to have lapsed when the prescribed period expired; and (b) lapses if it is not accepted within the extended period." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s37" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(5)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:b91a28293b2c879c780d7777a8bd8d87ee16227262ed0e31223d4168d6f28eec" ;
    tmk:ordinal 18 ;
    tmk:text "(5) For the purposes of this section, the use of a trade mark by a predecessor in title of an applicant for the registration of the trade mark is taken to be a use of the trade mark by the applicant." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s41(5)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44(4)> a tmk:LegislativeUnit ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:770d59d5f222c3ec181d5c980baf2929bd604747dd6b9d01bbea6538aca57448" ;
    tmk:ordinal 24 ;
    tmk:text "(4) If the Registrar in either case is satisfied that the applicant, or the applicant and the predecessor in title of the applicant, have continuously used the applicant’s trade mark for a period:" ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s44(4)" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s45> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Divisional applications"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:7be83e5257d68826159cc196e4e6a67ddbf27edd1510b5312e06df0c2b6bc2fc" ;
    tmk:text "(1) If a single application for the registration of a trade mark in respect of certain goods and/or services is pending (parent application), the applicant may make another application (divisional application) for the registration of the trade mark in respect of some only of the goods and/or services in respect of which registration is sought under the parent application. Note: For applicant and pending see section 6. (2) To avoid doubt, the parent application may itself be a divisional application. Note: A divisional application may be made by a person who has become the applicant in relation to the parent application because of subsection 108(2) (which deals with assignment and transmission)." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s45" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s71> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Notification of registration"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:c680bc2f9ad43c996b519157722d556115b27828715615b7c91c425da75d140f" ;
    tmk:text "When a trade mark has been registered, the Registrar must: (a) publish the registration in accordance with the regulations; and (b) give to the registered owner of the trade mark a certificate of registration in an approved form. Note: For registered owner and approved form see section 6." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s71" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s85> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Amendment to correct error or omission"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:a0408ab4ba378332bf7d225f73cced18c81cd48b711cb4ff02888ff0c729d65b" ;
    tmk:text "A prescribed court may, on the application of an aggrieved person, order that the Register be rectified by: (a) entering in the Register particulars that were wrongly omitted from it; or (b) correcting any error in an entry in the Register. Note: For prescribed court see section 190." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s85" .

