<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.5> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Components of notice of opposition"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMR1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:0db06dc0347d83754e1db06da626115db3759e2ff7fffaeb2a8e76c0f804431d" ;
    tmk:text "(1) The components of a notice of opposition are: (a) a notice of intention to oppose; and (b) a statement of grounds and particulars. (2) A notice of opposition is taken to be filed when both of its components have been filed." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMR1995/r5.5" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s16> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Definition of repealed Act"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:eed4282edbef05603a3f810f25e22ddf7bcbdf2f4510513d54c239a39ddcc622" ;
    tmk:text "(1) The repealed Act means: (a) the Trade Marks Act 1955 as in force immediately before its repeal; and (b) the regulations under that Act that were in force immediately before its repeal. Note: For the repeal of the Trade Marks Act 1955 see section 232. (2) In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears, a reference to a particular section of the repealed Act includes a reference to the regulations made for the purposes of that section and that were in force immediately before that Act was repealed." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s16" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s169> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "What is a certification trade mark?"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:db687655bb85f531bf98ecb4bb582257e1198a15401e1b1de39635449172a38f" ;
    tmk:text "A certification trade mark is a sign used, or intended to be used, to distinguish goods or services: (a) dealt with or provided in the course of trade; and (b) certified by a person (owner of the certification trade mark), or by another person approved by that person, in relation to quality, accuracy or some other characteristic, including (in the case of goods) origin, material or mode of manufacture; from other goods or services dealt with or provided in the course of trade but not so certified. Note: The goods or services certified may be those of any person, including the owner of the certification trade mark or any person approved by the owner for the purpose of certifying goods or services." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s169" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s203> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Exercise of power by Registrar"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:72f10fa763072143a7ded2d5068fced30b967c3d486f8f76606db7f31257e88a" ;
    tmk:text "The Registrar may not exercise a power under this Act in any way that adversely affects a person applying for the exercise of that power without first giving that person a reasonable opportunity of being heard." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s203" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s59> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Applicant not intending to use trade mark"@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:7af8c5f29c3242577fb2ab415e5034070f3c2d8b7a5a996c88a39ee9433ed9d2" ;
    tmk:text "The registration of a trade mark may be opposed on the ground that the applicant does not intend: (a) to use, or authorise the use of, the trade mark in Australia; or (b) to assign the trade mark to a body corporate for use by the body corporate in Australia; in relation to the goods and/or services specified in the application. Note: For applicant see section 6." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s59" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s97> a tmk:LegislativeProvision ;
    rdfs:label "Removal of trade mark from the Register etc. if application unopposed etc."@en-AU ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/doc/TMA1995> ;
    tmk:authorityKind "law" ;
    tmk:authorityStatus tmk:Current ;
    tmk:capturedIn tmk:snapshot-c490a9927f1a ;
    tmk:contentHash "sha256:4a66925d3b8f9edae54999dda0ea82a2a23e305685350dfd6d27b664b2472d22" ;
    tmk:text "(1) If: (a) there is no opposition to an application to the Registrar under subsection 92(1); or (b) an opposition to an application under that subsection has been dismissed (see section 99A); the Registrar must remove the trade mark from the Register in respect of the goods and/or services specified in the application. (2) If there is no opposition to an application to a court under subsection 92(3), the court must order the Registrar to remove the trade mark from the Register in respect of the goods and/or services specified in the application. The court must cause a copy of the order to be served on the Registrar and the Registrar must comply with the order." ;
    tmk:upstreamRef "TMA1995/s97" .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part11/1> a tmk:Page ;
    rdfs:label "Part 11.1. Applications in Australia (convention applications) where the applicant claims a right of priority"@en-AU ;
